      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_varcoeff_dirichlet_decay",
          "description": "Manufactured solution u(x,t) = exp(-4 pi^2 t) sin^2(pi x) + 0.5 for u_t = div(k(x) grad u) + S(x,t) with k(x) = 1 + 0.5 cos(2 pi x) and gL = gR = 0.5. Derivation: div(k grad u) = exp(-4 pi^2 t)[2 pi^2 cos(2 pi x) + pi^2 cos(4 pi x)] and u_t = exp(-4 pi^2 t)[-2 pi^2 + 2 pi^2 cos(2 pi x)]; the forcing S = u_t - div(k grad u) = exp(-4 pi^2 t)(-2 pi^2 - pi^2 cos(4 pi x)) matches the rhs term above, so u solves the continuous PDE exactly. sin^2(pi x) has zero value AND zero gradient at both walls, so the wall values are the constant 0.5 (prescribed as gL = gR = 0.5) and the mirror-ghost boundary flux carries no variable-coefficient cross term; the constant offset is discretely exact, so the error is the sin^2 mode's O(dx^2), clean 2nd order in both L2 and Linf. References evaluate at cell centers x_i = (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and the metaparameter N only; the constant 0.5 matches gL/gR, and the ic uses sin^2(pi x)+0.5 = 1 - 0.5 cos(2 pi x)). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the relative L2 discretization error, which falls at the conservative-FV order 2. Exact per-resolution error values are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/heat_1d_varcoeff_dirichlet/golden/errors.json.",
